# deploy/.env — per-host compose interpolation. Copy, don't edit this file:
#
#   cd Sim2RealLab/source/strafer_ros/deploy && cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored (repo convention: `.env.example` is committed, `.env` is
# per-machine). Docker Compose auto-loads `deploy/.env` because every compose
# file in this project lives here, so it sets the project directory.
#
# Compose expands `${VAR:-default}` from the host environment and this file at
# PARSE time. This is not an `env_file:` — nothing here reaches a container
# unless a service maps it. The deploy overlays use `${VAR:-default}` so a value
# can be driven from here without a service `environment:` key shadowing it.
#
# Confirm what a service actually gets:
#     docker compose <same -f/--profile flags> config
# and apply a change with `up -d --force-recreate <service>` — `restart` reuses
# the old container environment and applies nothing.

# --- models directory ---------------------------------------------------------
# Bind-mounted read-only at /models in the `inference` service. The default
# below is deploy/models/, which exists so the bind source is always a real path
# but ships EMPTY. Either stage the exported artifact (.onnx + .json sidecar)
# there, or point this at wherever it lives:
#
#   STRAFER_MODELS_DIR=/home/<user>/strafer_models
STRAFER_MODELS_DIR=./models

# --- policy selection ---------------------------------------------------------
# Unset here so each lane's own default stands (the sim-bridge overlay defaults
# to /models/policy.onnx + DEPTH_SUBGOAL + hybrid_nav2_strafer). Setting one
# overrides that lane without editing a tracked compose file — this is the
# supported model-swap lever.
#
#   STRAFER_INFERENCE_MODEL_PATH=/models/<artifact>.onnx
#   STRAFER_POLICY_VARIANT=DEPTH_SUBGOAL
#   STRAFER_NAV_BACKEND=hybrid_nav2_strafer

# --- diagnostics --------------------------------------------------------------
# Node-side obs dump for the parity harness. Read once at node init, so it must
# be set before the container starts. Depth variants write a full depth vector
# per tick (~2-3 MB/s) — captures only, never a normal mission. Needs the
# matching /obs_dumps bind in docker-compose.override.sim-bridge.yml.
#
#   STRAFER_OBS_DUMP_PATH=/obs_dumps/node_obs.jsonl

# --- SLAM scene keying --------------------------------------------------------
# The rtabmap database is keyed to the scene it was recorded under; a database
# from a different task/scene is refused at launch rather than reloaded. Bump
# the token per sim run — a procedural scene regenerates its layout on restart.
# Empty leaves the database unkeyed.
#
#   STRAFER_SLAM_TASK_ID=<task-id>
#   STRAFER_SLAM_SCENE_TOKEN=run4

# --- zenoh (remote-workstation convenience only) ------------------------------
# Must match the workstation's zenoh-bridge-ros2dds version.
#   ZENOH_TAG=1.5.1
